In article <balaji.760202183@yorku.ca>, balaji@nexus.yorku.ca (Balaji) says:
>
>I've read many boasts here lately about high-score ascensions (incl.
>a claim of 18M pts) but what about a low score ascension? Seems to me
>that's equally, if not more challenging.
>
>The easy part is: don't collect gems (except a few to ward off u's),
>keep your pets and everyone else away from you when standing on the
>endgame altar, drop all your stuff besides the AY when you #offer it.

If you keep your extra amulets in a BOH, and any stray cash in your
BOH, this is a very fast operation.  Of course, you can skip collecting
any gems at all (peaceful u's stay away from you already).  If you wanted,
you could even skip collecting $ (after all, bribing priests takes time)

>The other stuff that gets factored in is your *real* experience (i.e Xp
>gained by whacking monsters, rather than by other means) and the number
>of levels visited. You can keep down the levels visited by not going to
>the mines, not going on the quest (so you have to wish for the bell, and
>maybe the candles as well.)

If I'm not mistaken, the score for dungeon levels is Only based on the
deepest level you've visited.  I've had 3rd level barbarians level
teleport to dungeon level 22, and they got credit for that depth,
even if they didn't visit every level in between.  Since you have to
go to the deepest level (the Sanctum) anyway, visiting the Mines and
the Quest will not influence your score in this regard.  Just be sure
to let your pet kill the Quest Nemesis.

>To boost your HP while keeping your real Xp
>down, you have to run away from all monsters except wraiths and succubi,
>and quaff lots of PoGL.

Also, let your pet fight anything it can handle, and be ready to
throw potions at it to heal it (healing, gain and restore ability, etc.)

>So: how about some low-score boasts here? (I don't plan to participate
>in this challenge myself: I only ascended once, and that was after much
>huffing and puffing. 5M pts, incidentally.) What do you suppose is the
>theoretical lowest possible score?

There was a post recently about someone ascending with a score
somewhere around 750K.  I think he actually Intended to shoot for
the lowest score, by avoiding cash and combat whenever possible.
If you were playing a priest, and expected that you could get
3 wraith corpses on the Home level of your quest, then you would
only need to earn enough experience for 11th level (10K = 40K score).

If you were somehow able to get Medusa to stone herself, Orcus to
zap himself, and your pet to kill most other things, you might be
able to get by with (shot in the dark) another 40-50K XP (or 160-200K score)
You'd just have to avoid killing the WoY, demon lords, liches, and eels
as much as possible, keeping your pet to do the dirty work.

Doubling this total value (200-250K score) might get you a ballpark
of a possible 500K game.  Certainly the 750K was an admirable result!

